Description:
Electronic reporting layouts in Dynamics 365 finance and operations apps allow
for the creation and management of compliance-related reports and documents,
supporting regulatory requirements.

From the main menu, navigate to Budgeting > Setup > Budget control > Budget
control configuration; Apply document filtering as needed for budget control;
Click Save.

From the main menu, navigate to Budgeting > Setup > Budget control > Budget
control configuration; Apply document filtering as needed for budget control;
Click Save.

From the main menu, navigate to Procurement and sourcing > Setup > Vendors >
Vendor evaluation criteria; Add, edit, or delete evaluation criteria as needed;
Click Save.

From the supplier portal, click Register to begin the registration process;
Enter required company and contact information; Submit the registration request
for review.

From the main menu, navigate to Procurement and sourcing > Vendors > All
vendors; Select the vendor; Set the vendor status to Prospective (not approved);
Click Save.

From the main menu, navigate to Supplier Engagement app > Registration requests;
Review profile fields, contacts, addresses, tax IDs, banking, and certificates
for completeness and compliance.

From the main menu, navigate to Procurement and sourcing > Vendors > All
vendors; Click New to create an intercompany vendor for the receiving company;
Enter details and click Save.

From the main menu, navigate to Accounts receivable > Customers > All customers;
Click New to create an intercompany customer for the selling company; Enter
details and click Save.

From the main menu, navigate to Organization administration > Setup >
Intercompany trading relationships; Configure trading relationships as needed;
Click Save.

From the main menu, navigate to Organization administration > Setup >
Intercompany trading relationships; Link the vendor and customer as partners;
Click Save.

From the main menu, navigate to Organization administration > Setup >
Intercompany accounting; Configure intercompany accounting settings as needed;
Click Save.

From the main menu, navigate to Organization administration > Setup >
Intercompany accounting; Map ledger postings for intercompany transactions;
Click Save.

From the main menu, navigate to Procurement and sourcing > Vendors > All
vendors; Select the vendor; Click Vendor hold and set the appropriate hold type;
Click Save.

From the main menu, navigate to Accounts payable > Vendors > All vendors;
Enable/disable collaboration per vendor and set PO autoâ€‘confirm as needed;
Click Save.

From the main menu, navigate to Procurement and sourcing > Vendors > All
vendors; Select the vendor; Click Bank accounts; Select the account to update;
Click Edit, update details, and click Save.

From the main menu, navigate to Procurement and sourcing > Setup > Approved
vendor list; Add or remove vendor approvals at item/category level as needed;
Click Save.

From the main menu, navigate to Procurement and sourcing > Setup > Policies;
Ensure receipt and confirmation policies capture data for on time and in full
measures; Click Save.

From the main menu, navigate to Procurement and sourcing > Setup > Policies;
Confirm product receipt is posted with dates and quantities required for KPIs;
Click Save.

From the main menu, navigate to Procurement and sourcing > Vendors > All
vendors; Click Addresses; Select the address; Click Registration IDs and Add;
Enter details and click Save.

From the main menu, navigate to Procurement and sourcing > Price/discount
agreements; Click New to create a journal; Select vendor group as relation;
Click Save.

From the main menu, navigate to Procurement and sourcing > Price/discount
agreements; Use trade agreement journals to manage vendor-specific discounts;
Click Save.

From the main menu, navigate to Procurement and sourcing > Price/discount
agreements; Click New to create a journal; Select vendor group as relation;
Click Save.

From the main menu, navigate to Procurement and sourcing > Requests for
quotations > All RFQs; Add vendors to the RFI and send invitations as needed;
Click Save.

From the main menu, navigate to Procurement and sourcing > Requests for
quotations > All RFQs; Add vendors and allow bid revisions before deadline;
Click Save.

From the main menu, navigate to Syntex > Model gallery > Document processing;
Train a model to extract key fields (supplier, term, amount) for goods
contracts.

From the main menu, navigate to Syntex > Model gallery > Document processing;
Train a model to extract key fields (supplier, term, amount) for services
contracts.

From the main menu, navigate to Procurement and sourcing > Purchase requisitions
> All purchase requisitions; Add a category-based line for non-catalog items;
Click Save.

From the main menu, navigate to Procurement and sourcing > Purchase requisitions
> All purchase requisitions; Select item number, quantity, and delivery details;
Click Save.

From the main menu, navigate to Procurement and sourcing > Purchase requisitions
> All purchase requisitions; Open vendor punchout site and select products;
Click Save.

From the main menu, navigate to Procurement and sourcing > Purchase orders > All
purchase orders; Enter vendor linked to intercompany customer and set defaults;
Click Save.

From the main menu, navigate to Procurement and sourcing > Chargebacks >
Generate debit notes; Convert approved chargebacks into debit notes for posting;
Click Save.

From the main menu, navigate to Procurement and sourcing > Chargebacks >
Generate debit notes; Run process to create debit note linked to chargeback;
Click Save.
